:"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 2 cuisines","intro":[["The Scorpaenidae (also known as scorpionfish) are a family of mostly marine fishes that includes many of the world's most venomous species. As their name suggests, scorpionfish have a type of \"sting\" in the form of sharp spines coated with venomous mucus. They are widespread in tropical and temperate seas, especially in the Indo-Pacific region. They should not be confused with the cabezones, of the genus Scorpaenichthys, which belong to a separate, though related, family, Cottidae."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-scorpionfish"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scorpionfish"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine",[["Bouillabaisse","dish/bouillabaisse"]]],["New Caledonian cuisine","cuisine/new-caledonian-cuisine",[["Bouillabaisse","dish/bouillabaisse"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Crouton","ingredient/crouton"],["European conger","ingredient/european-conger"],["Fish","ingredient/fish"],["Olive oil","ingredient/olive-oil"],["Rouille","ingredient/rouille"],["Sea robin","ingredient/sea-robin"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"],["White wine","ingredient/white-wine"],["Wine","ingredient/wine"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/d/d2/Scorpionfish_Nick_Hobgood.jpg/500px-Scorpionfish_Nick_Hobgood.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Nhobgood","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Scorpionfish_Nick_Hobgood.jpg"}},"ingredient/white-onion":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/white-onion","n":"White onion","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["White onions are a cultivar of dry onion which have a distinct light and mild flavour profile. Much like red onions, they have a high sugar and low sulphur content, and thus have a relatively short shelf life. White onions are used in a variety of dishes, such as those of Mexican and European origin. Their uses in dishes often relate to their mild nature, they are often included in dishes to provide a light, fresh and sour taste to dishes and are often added uncooked to dishes such as salads."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-white-onion"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_onion"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Chicago-style hot dog","dish/chicago-style-hot-dog"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Celery salt","ingredient/celery-salt"],["Chicago-style relish","ingredient/chicago-style-relish"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Hot dog","ingredient/hot-dog"],["Kosher dill pickle","ingredient/kosher-dill-pickle"],["Mustard","ingredient/mustard"],["Mustard (condiment)","ingredient/mustard-condiment"],["Pickled cucumber","ingredient/pickled-cucumber"],["Poppy seed","ingredient/poppy-seed"],["Sport peppers","ingredient/sport-peppers"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"],["Vienna Beef","ingredient/vienna-beef"],["Vienna sausage","ingredient/vienna-sausage"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/9/95/White_onions_for_sale_in_supermarket.JPG/500px-White_onions_for_sale_in_supermarket.JPG","w":500,"h":362,"by":"Tomwsulcer","lic":"CC0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:White_onions_for_sale_in_supermarket.JPG"}},"dish/kabuli-pulao":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/kabuli-pulao","n":"Kabuli pulao","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Afghan cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Kabuli pulao (or pulaw) is a variety of pilaf made in Afghanistan and Uzbekistan. It is known in Afghanistan as Qābilī palaw, and in Uzbekistan as the Osh palov, with neither country referring to it by the